*.pyc
.venv/
.env
*.DS_Store
docs/gazettes/pdfs/

# docs/gazettes/text/ is INTENTIONALLY NOT ignored — text files have
# to be committed transiently so the gazettes-derive workflow can see
# them on its fresh runner, bundle into texts-NN.json shards, and
# delete the transient files (deletions captured via `git add -u` in
# the derive's commit step). See parliamentwatch-data for the
# canonical pattern of this split-phase + bundle-then-delete flow.
#
# Diagnosed 2026-05-15: the retry pass was writing text files but the
# old gitignore here threw them away before derive could see them —
# producing succeeded=N in commit MESSAGES while texts-meta.json
# stayed at 3 bundled records forever.
